# UI popups and overlays

When adding or editing **popups, modals, dropdowns, tooltips, or any overlay panel** in the client UI:

1. **Panels must not be transparent.** Use an explicit opaque background so content behind never shows through.
2. **Use the project standard** for the panel surface (same as "Recent orders" dropdown and auth tooltips):
   - Inline style: `style={{ backgroundColor: '#020617', opacity: 1 }}`
   - Do not rely only on Tailwind classes like `bg-slate-800` for overlay content; they can render semi-transparent in some contexts.
3. **Shadow:** Prefer `shadow-2xl shadow-black/70` for floating panels so they read clearly over the page.
4. **Positioning:** Place modal/dialog content so it does not overlap the header (e.g. use `pt-24` or `items-end pb-8` on the overlay container so the panel sits lower and avoids the auth/widget area).

## Example — modal content box

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — panel can look transparent
<div className="bg-slate-800 border border-slate-600 rounded-lg shadow-xl p-5">

// ✅ GOOD — explicitly opaque
<div
  className="border border-slate-600 rounded-lg shadow-2xl shadow-black/70 p-5"
  style={{ backgroundColor: '#020617', opacity: 1 }}
>
```

## Example — dropdown / tooltip

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — same opaque style for any overlay panel
<div
  className="absolute ... rounded-lg border border-slate-600 shadow-2xl shadow-black/70"
  style={{ backgroundColor: '#020617', opacity: 1 }}
>
```

Backdrop/scrim behind the panel (e.g. `bg-black/70`) may stay semi-transparent for dimming; the **content** panel on top must be opaque.
